SATQ("7fe7cf26",{"q":"<p>During the first part of an experiment, a ball was launched from a <span class=\"nw\"><svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 5.42 8.29\" style=\"width:0.66em;height:1.01em;vertical-align:-0.05em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#Gf\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0749)\"/><\/svg>-foot-tall<\/span> platform. The graph shows the height <span class=\"nw\"><svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 5.75 7.75\" style=\"width:0.7em;height:0.94em;vertical-align:-0.35em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#G10\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0695)\"/><\/svg>,<\/span> in feet, of the ball <svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 6.15 5.66\" style=\"width:0.74em;height:0.69em;vertical-align:-0.09em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#G2\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0535)\"/><\/svg> seconds after it was launched during the first part of the experiment.<\/p><p class=\"mfigp\"><img class=\"mfig\" alt=\"Figure\" width=\"644\" height=\"638\" style=\"width:29.99em\" src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\"><\/p><p>During the second part of the experiment, the ball was launched the same way, but from a platform that is <svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 5.1 7.95\" style=\"width:0.62em;height:0.96em;vertical-align:-0.01em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#G1\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0715)\"/><\/svg> feet shorter than the first platform. Which of the following graphs could represent the height <span class=\"nw\"><svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 5.75 7.75\" style=\"width:0.7em;height:0.94em;vertical-align:-0.26em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#G10\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0695)\"/><\/svg>,<\/span> in feet, of the ball <svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 6.15 5.66\" style=\"width:0.74em;height:0.69em;vertical-align:0em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#G2\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0535)\"/><\/svg> seconds after it was launched during the second part of the experiment?<\/p>","c":{"A":"<p class=\"mfigp\"><img class=\"mfig\" alt=\"Figure\" width=\"644\" height=\"639\" style=\"width:29.99em\" src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\"><\/p>","B":"<p class=\"mfigp\"><img class=\"mfig\" alt=\"Figure\" width=\"644\" height=\"638\" style=\"width:29.99em\" src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\"><\/p>","C":"<p class=\"mfigp\"><img class=\"mfig\" alt=\"Figure\" width=\"644\" height=\"639\" style=\"width:29.99em\" src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\"><\/p>","D":"<p class=\"mfigp\"><img class=\"mfig\" alt=\"Figure\" width=\"644\" height=\"638\" style=\"width:29.99em\" src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\"><\/p>"},"r":"<p>Choice B is correct. It's given that <svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 5.75 7.75\" style=\"width:0.7em;height:0.94em;vertical-align:-0.35em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#G10\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0695)\"/><\/svg> represents the height, in feet, of the ball <svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 6.15 5.66\" style=\"width:0.74em;height:0.69em;vertical-align:-0.09em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#G2\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0535)\"/><\/svg> seconds after it was launched. It's also given that during the first part of an experiment, a ball was launched from a <span class=\"nw\"><svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 5.42 8.29\" style=\"width:0.66em;height:1.01em;vertical-align:-0.05em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#Gf\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0749)\"/><\/svg>-foot-tall<\/span> platform. Therefore, the y-coordinate of the y-intercept of the given graph, <span class=\"nw\"><svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 5.42 8.29\" style=\"width:0.66em;height:1.01em;vertical-align:-0.05em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#Gf\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0749)\"/><\/svg>,<\/span> represents the platform height, in feet. During the second part of the experiment, the platform the ball was launched from was <svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 5.1 7.95\" style=\"width:0.62em;height:0.96em;vertical-align:-0.1em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#G1\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0715)\"/><\/svg> feet shorter than the platform in the first part of the experiment. It follows that the height of the platform in the second part of the experiment was <svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 23.3 8.29\" style=\"width:2.82em;height:1.01em;vertical-align:-0.05em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#Gf\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0749)\"/><use href=\"#G6\" transform=\"translate(7.92 4.76) scale(0.0716)\"/><use href=\"#G1\" transform=\"translate(18.59 0.5) scale(0.0716)\"/><\/svg> feet, or <svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 5.08 8.19\" style=\"width:0.62em;height:0.99em;vertical-align:-0.04em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#G14\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0739)\"/><\/svg> feet. Therefore, the y-coordinate of the y-intercept of the graph representing the second part of the experiment must be <span class=\"nw\"><svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 5.08 8.19\" style=\"width:0.62em;height:0.99em;vertical-align:-0.04em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#G14\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0739)\"/><\/svg>.<\/span> Only choice B satisfies this condition.<\/p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This could represent the graph if the ball were launched from a platform that was about <svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 5.25 8.19\" style=\"width:0.64em;height:0.99em;vertical-align:-0.13em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#G8\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0739)\"/><\/svg> feet shorter rather than <svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 5.1 7.95\" style=\"width:0.62em;height:0.96em;vertical-align:-0.1em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#G1\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0715)\"/><\/svg> feet shorter.<\/p><p>Choice C is incorrect. This could represent the graph if the ball were launched from a platform that was <svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 5.1 7.95\" style=\"width:0.62em;height:0.96em;vertical-align:-0.01em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#G1\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0715)\"/><\/svg> feet taller rather than <svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 5.1 7.95\" style=\"width:0.62em;height:0.96em;vertical-align:-0.01em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#G1\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0715)\"/><\/svg> feet shorter.<\/p><p>Choice D is incorrect. This could represent the graph if the ball were launched from a platform that was twice as tall rather than <svg class=\"mx\" viewBox=\"0 0 5.1 7.95\" style=\"width:0.62em;height:0.96em;vertical-align:-0.1em\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"expression\"><use href=\"#G1\" transform=\"translate(0.4 0.4) scale(0.0715)\"/><\/svg> feet shorter.<\/p>"});
